WEBVTT

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:06.490
Hey...
You get the feeling we’re lost?

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.620
How’d we even end up like this?

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:18.210
Was this our fate... all along?

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.840
Kojiro... Nyarth... Fare—

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:07.320
One week earlier...

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:10.530
This is a factory in Kuchiba City.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:16.820
Y’know, I really hate these
fiddly little jobs we take...

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.620
Our operation funds
have hit rock bottom.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:20.830
We don’t have a choice.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:25.830
Sometimes I wonder, meow... What’s our career?
Part-time work, or Team Rocket, meow?

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:33.550
Oh... I’m so tired.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:35.430
Huh?

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:37.930
Hey! Pikachu!

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:40.390
The brat boys!

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:41.390
Now’s our chance!

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:42.810
You’re mine, meow!

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:45.850
Pikachu!

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:50.230
Ta-daah!

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:52.030
Team Rocket!

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:54.110
Pikachu, we gotchu!

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:56.660
Not on my watch!
Lucario, I choose you!

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:58.830
Aceburn, go!

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:04.830
Straight from Team Rocket HQ...

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:06.500
Vending, come on!

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:14.970
Rocket...

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:16.090
Vending...

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:18.050
Sakaki’s grinning...

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:19.970
Secret!

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.680
What’re we gonna get?!

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:25.180
The Slacker Pokémon, Namakero!

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:27.690
The Lazy Pokémon, Kekking!

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:37.450
Hold on a sec!
“It’s fittingly titled the Slacker Pokémon”?!

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:40.030
And this one’s
the world’s laziest Pokémon!

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:41.450
Don’t worry, meow!

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:41.990
Hmm?

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:45.580
When they unleash all the energy
they’ve stored up while lazing around,

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:48.330
it’ll be super powerful, meow!

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:49.540
I like the sound of that!

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:50.960
So, what moves can they use?

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.340
Slack Off!

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:56.550
What’s your deal?!

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:59.090
You were supposed to attack!
Attack!

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:00.600
Huh?

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:02.180
We’re gonna go first, then!

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:03.720
Lucario! Aura Sphere!

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:03.720
Aceburn! Pyro Ball!

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:17.280
<i>What an awful feeling!</i>

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:26.750
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow...

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:30.960
Does this mean Matori’s going to
lecture us again?

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:34.130
I’m so sick of
writing apologies, meow...

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:37.510
“Why do you continue to fail?

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.590
“Go reflect on why you failed.”

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:42.510
Shut up,
you bowl-headed four-eyes!

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:47.850
Come to think of it, our vending Pokémon
were completely useless today.

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:48.680
Right, meow!

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:52.230
We failed because of
the vending Pokémon, meow!

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:55.230
Hey, you.

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:56.860
Whaddaya got to say for yourself?

00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:59.650
Why didn’t we get cooler Pokémon?

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:02.660
“The machine comes down to luck.

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:05.830
“Sometimes you get good pulls,
sometimes you get bad ones.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:09.540
“To change your luck
is to change your life.”?

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:12.250
“Everyone has equal opportunities.”?

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:14.840
Where’d all this deep
smarty-pants junk come from?

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.960
What’s wrong with you?!

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:21.880
Wait, meow!

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:23.220
I know!

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:27.060
If we follow it, it might lead us
to whoever fills that machine at HQ!

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:30.850
I’m not gonna be happy
till I give ‘em a piece of my mind!

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:32.020
Let’s go!

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:33.600
Yeah!

00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:43.160
Ahh, if only I could soar on the wind
and roam as free as these clouds...

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:46.990
Thinking about it, all we’ve done recently
is missions, missions, lectures, lectures...

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:48.620
Apologies, apologies...

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:51.210
And it wears you out,
doesn’t it...?

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:53.290
What a great feeling...

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:54.630
Huh?

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:59.960
The Cotton Bird Pokémon,
Tyltto, meow!

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.220
The blue bird Pokémon
that brings happiness!

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:03.760
That sounds great!

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:05.890
We’ll catch that Tyltto
and catch us some happiness!

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:07.970
This is bound to improve our luck!

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:09.720
<i>Here goes!</i>

00:06:12.230 --> 00:06:15.310
It’s using Dragon Breath, meow!

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:21.690
<i>What an awful feeling!</i>

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:30.660
At least the sea broke our fall...

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:33.160
<i>What a great feeling...</i>

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:38.790
Huh... Should’ve known
the Water Bird Pokémon Pelipper could swim.

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:40.210
Who cares?
Just chase it, meow!

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:40.800
Go!

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.720
Go, go, go, go, go!

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:49.390
It’s a Whaloh, meow!

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:04.360
Musashi!

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:05.610
Nyarth!

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:07.450
Sonansu!

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:12.750
So, we’re inside Whaloh right now?

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:15.290
I don’t want to think we are,
but... probably.

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:19.960
We’re lucky to still be alive
after being swallowed up like that, meow.

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:24.090
How come you’re having fun
swimming around?!

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:25.090
Ing around!

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:26.300
Huh? What?

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:27.260
What!

00:07:27.260 --> 00:07:28.930
Is somebody there?

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:30.680
Body there!

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:31.850
Who’s that?

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:34.390
The Music Note Pokémon,
Perap, meow.

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:36.310
Music Note? Perap?

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:45.400
Perap says it’s been living here
ever since it got swallowed, too, meow.

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:47.200
Ever since?
How long’s it been here?

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:51.830
As long as this ship has?!

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:52.830
Wha...?!

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:54.500
This rusted heap?

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:56.500
That had to have been ages ago!

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:59.000
If worst comes to worst,
we might end up looking like this...

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:00.750
No! Anything but that!

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:02.550
There’s gotta be something
we can do...

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:03.500
That’s it!

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:07.300
Pelipper still has
the Rocket Vending in its mouth!

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:10.930
I get it! There have to be some
super cool Pokémon in there, meow!

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:13.010
So we use those Pokémon to escape!

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:16.730
You wanna get outta here too,
don’t you?

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:18.810
Open up, you stubborn...!

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:25.070
“My mission is delivering
the Rocket Vending to agents who need it!

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:28.530
“Until then,
I’m never letting it out of my mouth.”?!

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:30.240
Drop the cool guy act, will ya?!

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:32.580
<i>We’re</i> agents who need it!

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:34.240
Open up!

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.670
All right!

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:44.550
We made it out!

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:45.630
What a great feeling, meow.

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:47.590
Great feeling, meow!

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:53.510
So, where are we?

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:56.470
All I see is ice...

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:58.230
I’m freezing, meow...

00:08:58.230 --> 00:08:59.350
Freezing, meow!

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:02.480
Bet you’re glad
you finally got out!

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:04.320
Pelipper!

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:07.070
We couldn’t have done it
without you! Thanks a ton!

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:08.070
Huh?

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:10.700
Weren’t we following Pelipper...?

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:11.700
Right, meow!

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:13.530
Hold it, meow!

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:15.660
Wait for us!

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:19.790
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow...

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.670
A Mammoo, meow!

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:25.840
How did things
end up like this, meow?

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:27.920
Just hang on,
this won’t take long.

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:37.680
Well, we lost Pelipper...

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:39.810
But I can see a village, meow.

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:42.850
But I’m so hungry
I’m losing my grip...

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:55.570
A-A warm firepla—

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:57.870
Freshly baked brea—

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:02.460
S-Some nice, hot sou—

00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:16.180
Where are we?

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:17.930
What’s wrong, Musashi?

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:20.350
What’s that?

00:10:22.020 --> 00:10:23.980
So much food!

00:10:23.980 --> 00:10:26.190
<i>Let’s dig in!</i>

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:27.770
This tastes great!

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:29.820
It’s warming me up!

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:34.280
You don’t have to be
in such a hurry to eat.

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:36.070
There’s plenty more
where that came from.

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:38.700
Oh, this is the best!

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:42.290
I don’t know who you are,
but we owe you our lives!

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:44.670
Huh? Where have I...?

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:48.290
Even if you asked,
usually I would never answer...

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:50.170
...but why don’t I consider this
an exception?

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:53.720
Even if you ask us
about “this” or “that”...

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:55.630
Usually, we would never answer.

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:57.470
But let’s consider this an exception!

00:10:57.930 --> 00:10:59.810
To protect the Earth from devastation.

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:01.600
To preserve the Earth’s peace.

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:05.140
Championing love and sincere evil.

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:06.980
We’re the cute, naughty villains.

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:08.440
Yamato!

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:09.860
Kosaburo!

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:12.610
The Team Rocket duo
soars through the universe!

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:16.110
Like shocking pink,
a rosy tomorrow awaits us!

00:11:16.490 --> 00:11:18.070
Just kidding!

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:20.620
<i>Yamato?!</i>

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:23.410
What are you doing
all the way out here?

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:25.160
Oh, I know!

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:28.040
You’re carrying out a Team Rocket mission
at this very moment, right?

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:30.880
Oh, you dummies.
I quit all that.

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:32.960
You quit? Never!

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:35.260
Team Rocket’s
not all there is to life.

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:37.050
Team Rocket’s...

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:38.760
...nyot all there is to life?

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:42.060
I was an elite,
nothing like you three,

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:47.520
but eventually I just got tired of the daily routine
of missions, lectures, and apologies.

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:49.520
Just like me, meow...

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:54.030
Now I’m running a café
and doing wood carving as a hobby.

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:57.780
Well, you can rest up here
until you’ve recovered your strength.

00:11:57.780 --> 00:11:59.570
No way we’re doing that!

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:02.870
We’re gonna work hard to repay you
for saving us, till we can call it even!

00:12:03.830 --> 00:12:05.580
If you really want.

00:12:13.340 --> 00:12:15.670
A meal after a hard day’s work...

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:17.800
What a great feeling!

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:21.890
I wouldn’t mind
living like this.

00:12:21.890 --> 00:12:22.680
Yeah.

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:25.640
But how did we end up here
in the first place?

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:27.600
Hmm...

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:32.310
Right, meow!

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:34.020
We were chasing Pelipper, meow!

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:37.320
We’ve repaid Yamato enough by now,
so let’s get after it!

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:39.610
Hold on!
We’re not even saying goodbye?

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:40.110
Huh?

00:12:40.110 --> 00:12:41.570
Oh, it’s just...

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:45.120
After she took such good care of us,
it seems rude to just abandon her...

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:48.710
Kojiro. If you want to stay here,
don’t let us stop you.

00:12:48.710 --> 00:12:49.790
Huh?

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:54.170
I saw you and Yamato
carving one of the crown caps you love.

00:12:54.170 --> 00:12:57.880
I’ve never seen you
look so happy before, meow.

00:12:58.340 --> 00:12:59.550
Oh, no, that was...

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:02.260
Team Rocket’s
nyot all there is to life.

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:04.850
You’ve worked so hard
for so long.

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:20.360
Kojiro! Farewell!

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:23.700
Musashi! Nyarth! Sonansu!

00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:42.220
What’s this?

00:13:42.220 --> 00:13:45.890
“Here, where the Ground-type ends
and the Water-type begins.”

00:13:45.890 --> 00:13:48.850
So this is land’s end, meow?

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:53.480
I wish my hunger would end, too.

00:13:56.190 --> 00:13:58.070
I smell something good, meow.

00:13:58.070 --> 00:13:59.360
Huh?

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:03.740
This is it, meow!

00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:06.620
Oh, so it was the scent of bread!

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:11.000
Meow?!

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:15.630
She looks just like my first love,
Madonnya, meow!

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:17.710
Oh, we have customers?

00:14:17.710 --> 00:14:18.250
Huh?

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:20.090
You!

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:21.220
Who are you?

00:14:22.550 --> 00:14:24.970
Even if you asked,
usually I would never answer.

00:14:24.970 --> 00:14:26.260
But why don’t I—?

00:14:25.220 --> 00:14:26.260
Ahh!

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:27.140
Kosanji!

00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:29.720
It’s Kosaburo! Kosaburo!

00:14:32.310 --> 00:14:34.520
What is this?
It’s so tasty!

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:36.480
It’s amazing, meow!

00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:38.980
Oh, it’s nothing...

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:39.820
You know, I—

00:14:39.820 --> 00:14:41.820
Yeah, we know.

00:14:41.820 --> 00:14:45.820
You got fed up with the missions, lectures,
and apologies and quit Team Rocket, right?

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:48.830
Hey, that was supposed to be a big reveal!
Let me say it myself!

00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:51.080
Yamato told us everything, meow.

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:53.370
Huh? You saw her?

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:54.250
Now...

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:57.040
Time to repay the favor
with some hard work, Kosaburo.

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:58.880
It’s Kosanji!

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:00.590
Huh? You got it right...

00:15:07.470 --> 00:15:09.300
A meal after a hard day’s work...

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:11.560
What a great feeling!

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:15.600
I wouldn’t mind living like this.

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:17.400
You’ve said it, meow.

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:21.780
But... How did we end up here
in the first place, meow?

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:27.740
Ahh!

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:30.700
We’ve repaid him by now,
so let’s keep chasing Pelipper!

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:32.080
Huh?! But...

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:36.250
Nyarth. If you want to stay here,
don’t let me stop you.

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:42.130
I saw you having fun
with that Madonnya lookalike.

00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:45.630
I’ve never seen you
look so happy before.

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:47.970
Oh, how should I put it?
That was...

00:15:47.970 --> 00:15:51.600
“Team Rocket’s
nyot all there is to life.” Right?

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:53.640
You’ve worked so hard, too...

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:55.270
You’ve worked really hard too, meow!

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:02.270
Nyarth! Farewell!

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:07.860
I stayed up late
sewing this, meow!

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:09.780
Take it, meow!

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:18.330
How far’s it gonna fly?

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:19.920
Huh?

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:24.960
What are you doing, Tyltto?!

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:28.220
Aren’t you supposed to be the
blue bird Pokémon that brings happiness?!

00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:37.560
What an awful fee— ling...

00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:50.240
Hey...
You get the feeling we’re lost?

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:55.950
How’d we even end up like this?

00:16:58.120 --> 00:17:01.120
Was this our fate... all along?

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:07.380
Kojiro... Nyarth... Fare—

00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:13.850
Musashi!

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:15.890
Get it together, meow!

00:17:15.890 --> 00:17:17.430
Huh? Why...?

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:19.640
Saving a friend in need...

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:21.900
..is what a true friend
does, meow!

00:17:21.900 --> 00:17:23.360
Kojiro... Nyarth...

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:24.400
That hurts, that hurts!

00:17:24.400 --> 00:17:26.780
I said that hurts!

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:28.360
Huh? A Sand?

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:32.490
Then what was that?
A dream?

00:17:34.070 --> 00:17:36.240
Sonansu! Wake up!

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:40.330
This ain’t the time to slack off
and drop dead, you hear me?!

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:43.380
We’re following that Pelipper,
no matter what it takes!

00:17:51.010 --> 00:17:51.760
No! No!

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:54.010
No! Somebody help me!

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:55.260
I can’t, I can’t...!

00:17:57.350 --> 00:18:00.270
I can’t do it...
I’m out of energy...

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:05.150
That’s right,
what was it Pelipper said?

00:18:05.150 --> 00:18:07.900
“To change your luck
is to change your life.”

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:13.030
Then I guess we were just
unlucky to the bitter end...

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:14.660
Musashi!

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:17.160
Kojiro? Nyarth?

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:21.160
What a stroke of luck it is
to see you again!

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:23.670
You guys...
Why are you here?!

00:18:24.170 --> 00:18:26.170
It’s a long story.

00:18:24.940 --> 00:18:29.540
Have you heard about this, meow?

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:31.470
The moment I took my eyes off it,
Morpeko ate the café out of all its food.

00:18:30.550 --> 00:18:34.990
Even when a cloudy night hides the stars and the planets

00:18:31.470 --> 00:18:36.930
Yamato tossed me out,
and when I saw Pelipper again, I chased after it!

00:18:36.270 --> 00:18:45.960
There’s still one, and only one you can still see

00:18:36.930 --> 00:18:43.690
And for me, that Madonnya lookalike turned out to be
good friends with the Persian who rules the town, meow...

00:18:43.690 --> 00:18:47.060
With a broken heart,
I bid the town farewell, meow.

00:18:46.750 --> 00:18:51.820
It’s right nearby, it’s just beneath your feet

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:51.820
That’s when I saw Kojiro
chasing after Pelipper, meow.

00:18:51.820 --> 00:18:54.070
Save the details for later...

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:56.070
Just do something already!

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:57.410
R-Right!

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:02.620
How’re you supposed to help
if you get stuck, too?!

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:04.120
Luck is still on our side!

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:05.960
Pelipper, help us, meow!

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:11.760
What? You don’t have room
for anything else?

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:14.510
Then just spit out
the thing in your mouth!

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:17.550
No, it’ll never let it go!

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:24.430
<i>What an awful feeling!</i>

00:19:32.780 --> 00:19:35.030
Y-You saved us...

00:19:37.910 --> 00:19:42.410
I don’t quite get it,
but do we owe it all to Pelipper?

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:44.080
The machine comes down to luck.

00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:46.460
Sometimes you get good pulls,
sometimes you get bad ones.

00:19:46.460 --> 00:19:49.130
Sometimes they’re good,
even if you think they’re bad.

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:51.550
And sometimes they’re bad,
even if you think they’re good.

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:54.420
And life rolls on
like a vending machine, meow.

00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:58.340
So...
How are we getting back home?

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:02.640
What’s wrong, Pikachu?

00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:03.680
<i>The brat boys?!</i>

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:04.850
Team Rocket!

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:07.060
I’ve got a good idea.

00:20:07.060 --> 00:20:09.600
Hey!
Say, “What are you guys up to?!”

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:12.020
Huh...?
What’re you guys up to?!

00:20:13.530 --> 00:20:16.400
If you ask us
“What’re you guys up to?!”

00:20:16.990 --> 00:20:19.660
We’ll answer out of
sympathy for the world!

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:23.490
To protect the world from devastation.

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:26.330
To preserve world peace.

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:29.790
Championing the evils
of truth and love.

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:32.540
We’re the lovely, charming villains.

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:33.920
Musashi!

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:35.010
Kojiro!

00:20:35.590 --> 00:20:38.470
The Team Rocket duo
soars through the galaxy!

00:20:38.470 --> 00:20:41.760
Like a white hole,
a white tomorrow awaits us!

00:20:41.240 --> 00:20:44.440
The “Ro” in “Team Rocket” stands for “Romanticism”!

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:44.180
Just kidding, meow!

00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:47.610
The “ke” in “Team Rocket” stands for “Keenness”!

00:20:47.610 --> 00:20:50.230
The little “c” in “Team Rocket” between the two stands for...

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:52.230
“‘Course, we’re villains!”

00:20:52.150 --> 00:20:54.820
Team Rocket
really is my life, after all!

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:53.680
“Come on, come at us!”

00:20:53.680 --> 00:20:57.240
“Clearly, Pikachu’s too strong, meow!”

00:20:54.820 --> 00:20:56.860
We’re taking that cool Pikachu!

00:20:56.860 --> 00:20:57.740
Right!

00:20:57.240 --> 00:21:00.370
“What an awful feeling!” we scream as we blast off again,

00:20:57.740 --> 00:20:59.400
Not if I can help it!

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:00.860
Pikachu, 100,000 Volts!

00:21:00.370 --> 00:21:03.630
and beneath us we see a little, tiny earth,

00:21:03.630 --> 00:21:06.860
forests, mountains and Pokémon...

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:08.710
Here it comes,
here it comes, here it comes...!

00:21:06.860 --> 00:21:11.720
They all blend together! What a great feeling!

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:14.130
<i>What an awful feeling!</i>

00:21:11.720 --> 00:21:14.840
Wherever we land,

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:18.070
we’ll have a meal to prepare ourselves for tomorrow

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:20.220
Wh-Why were they smiling...?

00:21:18.070 --> 00:21:21.240
We look up and see the shining moon

00:21:20.220 --> 00:21:21.260
Who knows?

00:21:21.240 --> 00:21:24.440
We look each other in the eye and laugh together

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:31.140
<i>All in all, what a great feeling!</i>

00:21:27.590 --> 00:21:34.050
We’re the invincible Team Rocket!

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:33.520
Sometimes you’re lucky,
and sometimes you’re unlucky.

00:21:34.050 --> 00:21:37.520
Scaring crying children into silence...

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:37.530
But you can never truly know
if you really are lucky or not.

00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:39.950
Team Rocket!

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:40.860
Either way,
Team Rocket....

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:43.070
Keep moving ahead, towards
tomorrow!

00:23:07.070 --> 00:23:09.530
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.530 --> 00:23:10.870
Go!

00:23:11.620 --> 00:23:13.830
Satoshi! Go!
It’s been a while!

00:23:13.830 --> 00:23:14.660
Māmane!

00:23:15.040 --> 00:23:17.170
So this Denryu
is part of the project?

00:23:17.170 --> 00:23:18.250
Yes!

00:23:18.250 --> 00:23:21.840
The Asteroid Explorer
Fiarrow2 Retrieval Project!

00:23:21.840 --> 00:23:23.170
Ooh!

00:23:23.170 --> 00:23:24.470
Let’s go, Denryu!

00:23:24.470 --> 00:23:27.010
Send the light of hope into space!

00:23:27.010 --> 00:23:28.180
Light, on!

00:23:29.180 --> 00:23:30.930
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:30.930 --> 00:23:34.020
Reach Into Space! Denryu’s Light!!
